WEBVTT

00:03.540 --> 00:05.640
<i>About a hundred years ago.</i>

00:06.280 --> 00:10.420
<i>This? Why this is the story of a little girl,</i>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.040
<i>who travelled beyond the Door of Destiny.</i>

00:16.820 --> 00:17.620
Nadja,

00:16.820 --> 00:17.620
NAAJA

00:18.180 --> 00:20.720
With your eyes

00:18.180 --> 00:20.720
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.720 --> 00:21.930
Nadja,

00:20.720 --> 00:21.930
NAAJA

00:21.930 --> 00:24.190
What do you see?

00:21.930 --> 00:24.190
Nani ga mieru

00:24.390 --> 00:27.270
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.390 --> 00:27.270
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.400 --> 00:29.610
The door to the future,

00:27.400 --> 00:29.610
Mirai no tobira

00:30.500 --> 00:33.740
That's what I'm searching for

00:30.500 --> 00:33.740
Sagashite iru

00:34.180 --> 00:40.700
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:34.180 --> 00:40.700
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:45.420
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:41.660 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:52.130
It could be so much more fun

00:48.920 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:55.630
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.210 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:59.350
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.050 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.440 --> 01:08.560
I will go waving

01:06.440 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:15.490
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:08.860 --> 01:15.490
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:18.200
But I won't look back

01:15.490 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:23.410
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.450 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:27.080
Nadja, Your smile

01:23.660 --> 01:27.080
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:30.420
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.080 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:33.550
Under the blue sky,

01:30.630 --> 01:33.550
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:36.380
I will find the place

01:33.550 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:40.600
where my future lies

01:36.970 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:52.820 --> 01:54.700
I'm not going to lose!

02:02.360 --> 02:04.240
Good luck, you two!

02:10.860 --> 02:12.280
I win!

02:21.500 --> 02:22.360
Damn it...

02:23.000 --> 02:25.500
Looks like I'm no match for Nadja after all!

02:34.840 --> 02:39.000
Nadja, The Door of Destiny!!

02:42.500 --> 02:45.500
Today will be the last time, that I'll be able to climb trees with you.

02:46.060 --> 02:46.740
Oliver...

02:47.840 --> 02:50.360
You'll be leaving this place tomorrow, right?

02:51.120 --> 02:54.620
I'm going to work hard when I get to London...

02:55.100 --> 02:57.040
Then I'll open up the biggest shop,

02:57.200 --> 02:58.280
in all of England.

02:59.460 --> 03:01.080
That's the spirit!

03:02.780 --> 03:03.800
Alex!?

03:04.080 --> 03:06.980
I thought you didn't like climbing trees...

03:07.820 --> 03:10.980
It's because I won't have any more chances to climb trees with you for a while.

03:13.820 --> 03:16.760
Nadja and I, are turing 13 soon.

03:17.520 --> 03:21.280
When that time comes, we'll be leaving this orphanage just like you, Oliver.

03:21.980 --> 03:24.080
The three of us, will be going our separate ways, won't we?

03:29.200 --> 03:31.640
But, we'll definetely meet again!

03:32.500 --> 03:36.920
That's because, we're all a family raised at the Applefield Orphanage!

03:42.300 --> 03:43.860
Family, huh?

03:44.980 --> 03:45.840
Yeah.

03:46.280 --> 03:49.300
Even when they're separated, family is...

03:49.640 --> 03:51.040
still family, right?

03:51.500 --> 03:52.400
Yeah!

03:54.760 --> 03:57.840
I'm...going over that hill tomorrow.

03:58.700 --> 04:01.980
London is on the other side of that hill...

04:02.220 --> 04:05.880
And beyond that, there is
an even bigger world!

04:06.040 --> 04:09.640
That goes on for miles and miles...!

04:17.280 --> 04:20.480
<i>To Father and Mother in heaven,</i>

04:21.140 --> 04:23.340
<i>I'm doing fine today too.</i>

04:39.740 --> 04:40.860
Nadja!

04:40.920 --> 04:42.340
Nadja!

04:43.000 --> 04:44.540
Ms. Evans!

04:44.780 --> 04:47.040
The chairlady is looking for you!

04:47.080 --> 04:48.380
Looking for you!

04:48.660 --> 04:49.940
Miss Appleton is?

04:50.680 --> 04:54.240
Come on! Oliver and Alex!
You have to go get ready now.

04:54.700 --> 04:56.020
Get ready!

04:57.360 --> 04:58.420
Nadja...

04:58.580 --> 05:01.120
Something that was addressed to you was just delivered here.

05:01.600 --> 05:02.400
For me?

05:03.200 --> 05:04.480
Open it up and see.

05:04.680 --> 05:08.140
It may be something very important to you.

05:08.280 --> 05:08.700
Yes.

05:25.140 --> 05:26.760
Wow...

05:35.780 --> 05:37.420
It's beautiful.

05:37.920 --> 05:40.700
I've never seen... a dress like this before!

05:41.640 --> 05:42.940
What's this?

05:43.040 --> 05:44.300
A diary?

05:46.260 --> 05:48.140
There's a letter inside!

05:53.480 --> 05:56.020
Congratulations, Nadja!

05:56.380 --> 05:59.620
Soon, it will be your 13th birthday.

06:00.180 --> 06:01.940
To congratulate you...

06:02.000 --> 06:03.160
...your...

06:04.780 --> 06:09.700
I'm sending you your Lady Mother's... memento of her first ball!

06:11.540 --> 06:15.960
I'm wishing in my dreams that...you and your Mother will be together again.

06:17.800 --> 06:19.760
"your Lady Mother"...?

06:20.520 --> 06:22.280
"be together again"...?

06:23.000 --> 06:24.780
What's going on?

06:25.540 --> 06:29.260
My mother... is alive?

06:29.520 --> 06:31.360
The one that sent that,

06:31.720 --> 06:34.200
is probably the same person
that handed you over to me.

06:35.900 --> 06:37.640
You were...

06:37.660 --> 06:41.140
handed over to me while I was on a trip to Paris.

06:41.200 --> 06:43.340
That person was my mother?

06:43.480 --> 06:47.180
No. It was someone whom your mother knew.

06:47.920 --> 06:49.940
Your father had passed away.

06:50.200 --> 06:53.160
Your mother was weak from an illness.

06:53.300 --> 06:56.480
"There is no way she could raise a child..."

06:56.540 --> 06:58.420
Was what that person said.

07:00.080 --> 07:03.660
That brooch that you were wearing
when you were handed to me,

07:04.140 --> 07:07.060
and the dress and the diary
which were sent you...

07:07.800 --> 07:11.360
are all important things which
connect you and your mother.

07:14.920 --> 07:19.240
Wouldn't it be wonderful
if you could meet your mother someday?

07:22.460 --> 07:23.360
Yes!

07:26.720 --> 07:29.320
Mother... is alive somewhere!

07:31.080 --> 07:34.040
<i>I might be able to meet my mother someday.</i>

07:35.080 --> 07:37.880
Nadja? Nadja!

07:39.160 --> 07:40.420
What's wrong?

07:40.840 --> 07:41.600
Eh?

07:41.960 --> 07:43.600
Everyone's gone already.

07:43.840 --> 07:45.040
Let's hurry up and get going.

07:45.640 --> 07:46.240
Yeah...

07:47.820 --> 07:49.460
You know, I...

08:04.120 --> 08:05.360
It's a car!

08:12.940 --> 08:15.600
Ladies and gentlemen!

08:16.180 --> 08:18.200
Boys and girls!

08:18.600 --> 08:20.200
We come bringing love, dreams and hope!

08:20.240 --> 08:23.340
We are the Dandelion Troupe!

08:27.220 --> 08:28.860
It's showtime!

09:28.400 --> 09:30.120
Stars, onto the stage!

09:34.600 --> 09:37.260
The lovely singing princess, Silvie!

09:38.840 --> 09:41.800
The melancholy violinist, Thomas!

09:43.060 --> 09:45.620
Our laugh department, Abel!

09:46.900 --> 09:50.080
The world's smallest lion tamer, Rita!

09:51.400 --> 09:54.680
The twin lions, Crème and Chocolat!

09:55.440 --> 09:56.840
And then, there's me.

09:56.920 --> 10:00.740
The kindhearted strongman, Master George!

10:00.940 --> 10:04.220
Hello, hello, how are you,

10:04.260 --> 10:07.820
People of England?

10:08.020 --> 10:11.500
Bonjour, bonjour, how are you,

10:11.620 --> 10:14.780
People of France?

10:15.240 --> 10:18.500
Buenas tardes, how are you,

10:18.700 --> 10:22.060
People of Spain?

10:22.160 --> 10:25.760
Buon giorno, buon giorno, how are you,

10:25.820 --> 10:28.820
People of Italy?

10:29.220 --> 10:32.600
Lalala-lala, lalala-lala, lala-let's dance!

10:32.740 --> 10:36.340
Lalala-lala, lalala-lala, lala-let's sing!

10:36.420 --> 10:40.180
Girls and boys. Ladies and gentlemen.

10:40.340 --> 10:43.500
Welcome, welcome to the world of dreams!

10:45.280 --> 10:47.240
That dance looks like so much fun!

10:47.340 --> 10:50.680
How do you do, how do you do? Nice to meet you,

10:49.020 --> 10:50.240
Let's see

10:50.660 --> 10:53.840
People of Canada.

10:52.060 --> 10:54.480
I see. I get it!

10:54.620 --> 10:57.340
Sobh Bekheir, Nice to meet you,

10:57.400 --> 11:01.240
People of Persia.

10:57.420 --> 10:58.280
Nadja!

10:58.320 --> 10:58.900
Huh?

10:59.700 --> 11:01.420
Can you teach me too?

11:01.640 --> 11:04.720
Lalala-lala, lalala-lala, lala-let's dance!

11:01.700 --> 11:03.120
Teach me, teach me!

11:04.160 --> 11:05.420
Watch closely.

11:04.840 --> 11:08.200
Lalala-lala, lalala-lala, lala-let's sing!

11:05.520 --> 11:06.720
You do this...

11:06.820 --> 11:07.880
Then this!

11:08.400 --> 11:11.540
Girls, boys, messieurs, mesdemoiselles

11:08.960 --> 11:11.160
Like this?

11:11.780 --> 11:15.360
Here and everywhere in the world, we're all friends!

11:11.960 --> 11:13.040
Not like that.

11:13.460 --> 11:14.740
Like this!

11:15.860 --> 11:16.960
<i>Oh?</i>

11:17.700 --> 11:19.920
<i>She's pretty good, that young lady.</i>

11:34.040 --> 11:34.880
Wait!

11:44.020 --> 11:45.140
Miss?

11:47.540 --> 11:48.980
Just as I thought!

11:50.120 --> 11:54.320
You're a child who is loved
by the Goddes of Fate.

11:55.960 --> 11:56.840
Umm...

11:58.960 --> 12:00.980
I can tell.

12:01.480 --> 12:02.660
That's right!

12:02.940 --> 12:06.220
You're a child who will
follow a wondrous fate...

12:06.280 --> 12:09.480
which no one could have imagined.

12:11.200 --> 12:13.140
Hey, Granny!

12:22.080 --> 12:22.960
Umm...

12:23.980 --> 12:24.720
Bye.

12:32.160 --> 12:33.540
A wondrous fate?

12:36.280 --> 12:38.600
There she is, Rosso.

12:47.300 --> 12:50.260
It's unmistakable, right Bianco?

12:52.620 --> 12:56.220
That girl is the Nadja we're looking for.

13:18.040 --> 13:22.480
Hold in the palm of your hand the smiles

13:23.180 --> 13:28.260
Of the sun of this passing day

13:29.060 --> 13:33.940
Good night, good night

13:34.440 --> 13:37.560
As I hold you

13:38.040 --> 13:42.770
My darling child

13:51.920 --> 13:52.800
Good night.

14:38.880 --> 14:40.340
Mother's diary.

14:46.040 --> 14:47.800
It's in a foreign language...

14:56.520 --> 14:59.000
- Come, Bianco.
- Okay.

15:02.800 --> 15:03.920
It's beautiful.

15:04.700 --> 15:08.060
I wonder, what this ball Mother
went to was like?

15:11.500 --> 15:13.900
Was she about my age when she went?

15:15.180 --> 15:16.100
Wrong one.

15:17.640 --> 15:19.100
This is the wrong one too.

15:21.420 --> 15:22.380
Toilet...

15:41.600 --> 15:42.220
Huh?

15:46.800 --> 15:47.980
Thieves!

15:48.220 --> 15:49.060
Wait!

15:51.700 --> 15:52.840
What's wrong?

15:53.800 --> 15:54.900
What is this?!

15:56.100 --> 16:00.340
Peter! Phoebe! Daisy! Daniel!

16:00.440 --> 16:01.900
Nadja!

16:01.980 --> 16:03.460
Everyone!

16:04.120 --> 16:04.940
Daisy!

16:05.240 --> 16:06.900
Come on, over here!

16:08.940 --> 16:11.020
Everyone, wake up! It's a fire!

16:11.320 --> 16:12.420
What is it!?

16:12.720 --> 16:13.960
What is going on!?

16:14.220 --> 16:16.180
Governess, it's a fire!

16:16.420 --> 16:17.940
Hurry, get everyone outside!

16:26.660 --> 16:28.760
- George!
- Huh?

16:28.940 --> 16:30.780
- Look!
- Huh?

16:31.320 --> 16:32.340
A fire!?

16:41.880 --> 16:45.220
- Alex, is everyone accounted for?
- Yes!

16:45.300 --> 16:46.300
Give me a hand!

16:52.300 --> 16:53.740
Is everoyne alright?!

16:55.320 --> 16:56.640
We're going to help too!

16:57.640 --> 17:00.240
If we just stand around, everything will burn down!

17:00.700 --> 17:01.400
Yes!

17:03.140 --> 17:04.800
Ah, oh no!

17:05.200 --> 17:06.160
The trunk!

17:39.980 --> 17:41.980
We've found you, Nadja!

17:42.140 --> 17:42.780
Huh?

17:45.080 --> 17:45.960
Who are you?

17:47.040 --> 17:49.100
Hand over that brooch!

17:50.000 --> 17:50.980
This brooch?

17:51.730 --> 17:52.440
Why?!

17:52.550 --> 17:53.700
Just do it!

17:53.760 --> 17:54.960
Hand it over!

17:57.500 --> 17:59.260
What's up with those guys?!

17:59.500 --> 18:01.120
Why are they after the brooch?

18:02.020 --> 18:03.500
Be careful now!

18:03.700 --> 18:04.820
Hurry up! Hurry up!

18:26.140 --> 18:27.700
Hand that over!

18:27.820 --> 18:28.700
No!

18:28.860 --> 18:30.300
You little...!

18:30.860 --> 18:31.800
Stop it!

18:31.860 --> 18:33.860
This is my Mother's...

18:34.000 --> 18:36.140
Shut up! Hand it over!

18:42.080 --> 18:42.940
A ring?

18:43.140 --> 18:44.880
You gave us trouble.

18:46.420 --> 18:47.800
Give it back!!

18:50.260 --> 18:51.580
Give it back!!

19:07.400 --> 19:08.720
Who are you?!

19:11.320 --> 19:13.500
A moon... as beautiful as the one on this night...

19:14.540 --> 19:16.900
does not wish to see a lady's tears.

19:17.680 --> 19:19.700
Shut the hell up!

19:34.960 --> 19:36.220
Are you hurt anywhere?

20:00.120 --> 20:02.780
Never... hand this over to anyone.

20:03.360 --> 20:04.040
Huh?

20:11.320 --> 20:14.540
I'm... so scared!

20:20.360 --> 20:21.260
It's alright.

20:23.040 --> 20:25.280
It's alright... now.

20:45.680 --> 20:47.640
Such deep eyes...

20:49.220 --> 20:52.800
Like so many stars twinkling...

20:54.580 --> 20:56.320
As if he's...

20:56.380 --> 20:57.820
a star-eyed...

20:58.380 --> 20:59.720
knight...

21:16.240 --> 21:17.500
What's the matter?

21:18.420 --> 21:20.120
She's being chased by some bad people.

21:20.660 --> 21:21.920
Please shelter her.

21:30.320 --> 21:34.220
The townsfolk seems to have finally noticed the fire...

22:01.160 --> 22:06.380
I'm afraid, the Door of Destiny has opened, hasn't it...

22:14.490 --> 22:17.740
Paris is sunnier than London

22:14.490 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:27.540
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:21.370 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
Indeed

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
It's not use worrying about it

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:38.630
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:35.500 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:43.600
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:38.890 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
To be, to be

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:50.400
The tree fog won

22:45.390 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:54.780
The world frog-jumping contest

22:50.860 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:04.160
Under the kitten's paw

22:57.990 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:10.750
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:04.580 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:16.920
Paris is sunnier than London

23:13.590 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:26.890
It's not the time to hang around

23:20.510 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:32.270
Indeed, indeed

23:27.770 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:40.500 --> 23:42.100
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:42.400 --> 23:43.310
Amazing!

23:43.440 --> 23:45.860
Dancing can be this much fun?

23:46.230 --> 23:48.740
I ended up travelling with the Dandelion Troupe.

23:49.280 --> 23:52.160
I was so full of uncertainty and hope, that I couldnt sleep

23:52.660 --> 23:55.160
So I took a short walk around London at night.

23:55.410 --> 23:57.620
Eh? What's with this black-caped man?

23:58.200 --> 24:00.040
Saying, "Skinny girl"...

24:00.290 --> 24:02.420
Geez! How impolite is that?

24:02.540 --> 24:05.540
Tomorrow's Nadja, Night of The Phantom Thief 'Black Rose'

24:05.670 --> 24:07.800
Now, the Door of Destiny Opens.
